#11200
"Narrow Canyon Trail"
"This trail, barely wide enough to lead a horse through, winds through a canyon
set deep into a cliff.  The trail is littered with small rocks, and the cliff
walls are scored with weed-choked crevices.  The cliff walls show signs of
trauma, as if the path has only recently been uncovered.  Heavy timbers
suspended far above show that efforts have been made to shore up the passage
for safety's sake.  To the south, the latter part of the Great North Road can
be seen, while the trail continues to the north.
"
"*H
"
