#11202
"Widening of the Trail"
"At this point the trail from the south widens considerably.  While to the
south, a narrow pass through the cliffs can be seen, here the space is much
less claustrophobic.  Small, scrubby bushes are strewn about the trail, and
cling to the lower regions of the cliffs to the south, where they are offered
a degree of protection from the winds gusting through the pass.  A stream bed
cuts west through the trail at this point, but seems to have been devoid of
water for some years.  In the foothills past the cliff to the east, far-off
ruins can be seen, scattered shells of columned buildings left to the elements.
"
"[Hedrack] Is the cliff east up or down? Can we see over it?
"
