#11204
"Wilderness Fringe"
"The solid cliff face to the west seems somewhat lower at this point, but would
still be extremely dangerous to scale.  Dry bushes and shrubs scatter the
ground, indicating that slightly more water may be available to them here, but
that in recent times living has been hard in this wilderness.  To the north,
forestland can be glimpsed, appearing to comprise mainly of the hardier
varieties of conifer and pine.  This band of scrubland seems to separate the
cliffs and the pass to the south from the forested area northward.
"
"*H
