#11205
"Abandoned Northerly Road"
"The most southern part of this road is in the worst shape of all.  In some
places the stones have been torn up, exposing the foundation and layers of
sand beneath, and in others the rocks are piled as high as a man's waist.  The
piles are coated with moss and lichen, and some with small stunted bushes
clinging to the surface, forcing roots into available crevices.  A sapling
grows from a particularly large hole in the road, reaching stunted limbs
upward.
"
"*H
"
