#11206
"Edge of the Old Forest"
"From the smaller, scrubby trees and bushes south, and the larger and more
densely wooded area to the north, this would appear to be the edge of the
forest.  Pine needles are strewn about the ground, giving the sounds of forest
creatures muted tones.  Shattered flagstones, covered in moss and lichen, are
partially submerged in the carpet of needles, appearing to have been torn from
the road eastward at some point in the past.
"
"*H
