#11207
"Wilderness Fringe"
"A stream bed running from the east ends here in a shallow depression, which is
as dry as a desert.  A rocky outcrop which may at one point have been part of
the cliffs to the south lies west, an insurmountable obstacle.  Beyond these
rocks the walls of the cliff rise, giving the impression that you are in fact
in a valley.  Moss and scrubby, misshapen trees cover the boulders, appearing
to subsist on nothing more than the air surrounding them.  The ground is dry
and cracked, as if this region has not seen much water in some years.
"
"*H
"
