#11208
"Old Forest"
"The undergrowth here thickens, and the trees to the west are so closely packed
and overgrown that travel there is impossible.  This part of the forest
appears devoid of the cracked and ruined masonry found elsewhere, unless they
have been totally reclaimed by nature.  The trees here are tall, with many
thick branches at ground level, thinning out somewhat as the trunks grow more
slender.  The dense foliage above gives the forest a hushed, twilit feel even
in daylight.
"
"*H
