#11209
"Old Forest"
"The forest here is fairly thick, with no defined pathways or passages.  Tree
roots and boughs encroach on the ruined road to the east, cracking huge stone
slabs and forcing their way into masonry.  Ruined blocks are scattered here,
torn from the road by sheer force, now blanketed with moss.  Scrubby bushes
line the border with the road, while further to the west the forest grows
thicker and more inhospitable.
"
"*H
