#11210
"Abandoned Northerly Road"
"Indiscriminate piles of broken rubble, comprised of the heavy cobble and
flagstones torn from the road, are gathered in several places on the ground.
Vegetation from the forest to the west encroaches on the remnants of the road,
with roots breaking stone and creating cracks in those patches of road that
remain.  Part of a huge rounded column lies on the east side of the road,
having probably rolled down from one of the ruins visible on the hills to the
east.  It lies canted in its final resting place; a large hole made after
several layers of stone were removed from the road's eastern edge.
"
